    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0697" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6359 Wolfram Ore/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-08-12T12:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1933—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>281. Your 657, August 9, 9 a.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d640-f1"/> In conversations
                    in New York on August 6 and 7 with Soong, officer of the Department took
                    occasion to comment adversely on the grant of a monopoly for export of wolfram.
                    Soong expressed the view that the principle involved in the action taken by
                    Chinese authorities was wrong and said he would see what he could do about
                    rectifying the situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
